# Datasets are never committed. The split manifest in reports/ records the
# exact bytes used for any reported result; the pixels themselves stay out.
/data/
/artifacts/
/.tmp/
*.zip
*.tar.gz
CamVid/

# Model artefacts
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
checkpoints/

# Generated figures and the rendered report. Both are rebuilt in one command
# (`scripts/evaluate.py` then `scripts/report.py`), and the HTML embeds every
# figure as a data URI, so committing it would add ~600KB per regeneration for
# no information the JSON alongside it does not already carry.
reports/figures/
reports/report*.html

# The JSON in reports/ IS committed on purpose: it is the evidence behind the
# claims in README.md and docs/AUDIT.md, and it is small.

# Training artefacts
predictions/
runs/

!docs/assets/
